  "description": "Gemini 4 Carbon is Google DeepMind's strongest Gemini 4 reasoning model, built for sustained agentic workflows across complex software engineering, multimodal knowledge work, scientific reasoning, and cybersecurity defense. It was announced on 2026-10-28 and became generally available on 2026-11-10 on the Gemini API paid tier (model id gemini-4-carbon) and in Google AI Studio; it is not available on the free tier. It shares a 1,048,576-token unified context window with Gemini 4 Argon and supports long decodes up to 1M tokens, with thinking levels low, medium, and high (default medium). On hard problems Carbon spends more thinking tokens per turn than Argon. Introductory Gemini API and Vertex AI global pricing is $2.00 per million input tokens, $10.00 per million output tokens (including thinking tokens), and $0.10 per million cached input tokens through 2026-11-30; standard pricing of $4.00/$20.00/$0.20 begins 2026-12-01. Explicit caching is not supported (implicit caching only). Vertex AI non-global regions are billed at a 10% premium. A Cyber Permissive variant exists on Vertex AI at the standard (non-introductory) rate and is not cataloged as a separate model.",
